From fb6e1ad735d0a70c0bc5a5ac7cb8ec1617139055 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Govindarajulu Varadarajan <govindarajulu.varadarajan@amd.com>
Date: Thu, 2 Oct 2025 20:11:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 152/190] xilinx-ai-engine: do not use mutex_lock_interruptable
 in clean up path

commit b4dfb4e6db35dfb46eb70edda6d924c7478fcfbb from
https://github.com/Xilinx/linux-xlnx.git xlnx_rebase_v6.12

During clean and removal of a partition, if the userspace application
receives a signal, the clean up kernel thread exits without clean up and
removal. This results in stale partition and no way to remove it.
Subsequent partition create will fail with partition already exists.

Signed-off-by: Govindarajulu Varadarajan <govindarajulu.varadarajan@amd.com>
Acked-by: Gregory Williams <gregory.williams@amd.com>
Message-ID: <20251003031202.2319372-13-govindarajulu.varadarajan@amd.com>
State: pending
Signed-off-by: Quanyang Wang <quanyang.wang@windriver.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
